{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/stronglyconnectedcomponents()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The strongly connected components: maximal sets of vertices each reaching every other."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Tarjan’s algorithm, iterative, O(V + E)."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stronglyConnectedComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity10ComponentsV","text":"Components","identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Components are in the order Tarjan’s algorithm completes them, on a depth-first search"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with roots in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order and successors in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" order (the order of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"NetworkX, petgraph and Boost). That is a reverse topological order of the condensation:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every edge between components goes from a later component to an earlier one, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reversed()"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the components with every edge going forward. Each component lists its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order."}]